const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"解释历史与提前预测分开",en:"Explaining history differs from forecasting ahead"},body:{zh:"Goyal与Welch比较多种文献中的权益溢价预测变量，重点追问模型在当时可用的信息下能否胜过简单基准。用全样本估计出的关系能够描述过去，并不说明每个历史时点都能得到同样的参数或预测。",en:"Goyal and Welch compare published equity-premium predictors against a simple benchmark using information available at the forecast date. A relation fitted to the full history may describe the past without being a forecast that could have been produced at each date."},reference:{url:"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w10483/w10483.pdf",label:{zh:"2004年5月NBER版 · §1",en:"May 2004 NBER edition · §1"}}},{title:{zh:"历史均值也必须只用当时的历史",en:"The historical mean must also be available at the time"},body:{zh:"基准不是研究结束后才算出的全样本平均值，而是随着预测时点推进、利用此前数据得到的历史均值。模型和基准必须在相同信息范围下比较。编辑建议同时保存两个预测序列，不能只报告模型自身的样本内拟合优度。",en:"The benchmark is the mean available from prior observations at each forecast date, not the final full-sample average. Model and benchmark must share the same information boundary. Editorial application: retain both forecast sequences rather than reporting only the model's in-sample fit."},reference:{url:"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w10483/w10483.pdf",label:{zh:"2004年5月NBER版 · §1",en:"May 2004 NBER edition · §1"}}},{title:{zh:"借用过的测试期不再完全陌生",en:"A previously studied test period is not wholly unseen"},body:{zh:"文章指出，即使计算过程称为样本外评价，研究者仍可能已经知道某段历史的表现，或根据既有研究选择变量。这个问题不靠重新切一次数据就自动消失。编辑建议保留变量选择、修改和评价的记录，不把形式上的留出样本说成全新证据。",en:"A computational out-of-sample exercise may still use a period familiar to researchers or variables chosen through earlier studies. Repartitioning alone cannot undo that prior knowledge. Editorial application: retain the history of selection and revisions instead of calling every holdout entirely new evidence."},reference:{url:"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w10483/w10483.pdf",label:{zh:"2004年5月NBER版 · §1",en:"May 2004 NBER edition · §1"}}},{title:{zh:"权益溢价需要股票与无风险两端",en:"An equity premium needs both equity and risk-free inputs"},body:{zh:"权益溢价由股票收益与对应期间的无风险收益共同构成。价格收益、含分红收益及不同期限利率并不等价；数据源和历史替代序列会影响可比性。下方复权教程只处理价格准备，不提供本文完整的股息、利率或早期历史输入。",en:"An equity premium combines equity returns with a corresponding risk-free return. Price returns, dividend-inclusive returns and yields of different maturities are not interchangeable. The linked tutorial prepares adjusted prices only, not the paper's full dividend, interest-rate or early-history inputs."},reference:{url:"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w10483/w10483.pdf",label:{zh:"2004年5月NBER版 · §2",en:"May 2004 NBER edition · §2"}}},{title:{zh:"D/P与D/Y标签背后是不同价格日期",en:"DP and DY use different price dates"},body:{zh:"工作论文区分股息价格比DP与股息收益率DY：两者采用的价格日期不同，一个对应当前价格，另一个使用滞后价格。名称相近不代表预测信息相同。编辑建议将公式、滞后期与发布时间直接写入变量合同，而不是仅保存缩写。",en:"The working paper distinguishes DP from DY through the date of the price denominator: current versus lagged price. Similar labels do not imply identical predictive information. Editorial application: preserve the formula, lag and availability date rather than storing an acronym alone."},reference:{url:"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w10483/w10483.pdf",label:{zh:"2004年5月NBER版 · §2",en:"May 2004 NBER edition · §2"}}},{title:{zh:"结论跟着样本、期限与版本走",en:"Conclusions travel with the sample, horizon and edition"},body:{zh:"初始训练窗口、预测期限、变量定义和样本终点都会影响评价。这份早期稿与后来的期刊版不能仅凭标题相近就混用数值。编辑建议引用具体版本，并将历史发现与新的市场测试分开，避免把一次负面结果写成普遍的不可能定理。",en:"Training windows, horizons, variable definitions and sample endpoints affect the comparison. Numerical results from this early manuscript should not be silently merged with the later journal article. Editorial application: name the edition and distinguish historical findings from tests in a new market."},reference:{url:"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w10483/w10483.pdf",label:{zh:"2004年5月NBER版 · §1–2",en:"May 2004 NBER edition · §1–2"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"依据2004年工作论文阅读预测评价方法，正式期刊引用不变。历史样本中的预测困难不能外推成任何市场、任何时期都不存在可预测性。",en:"This guide uses the 2004 working paper to explain forecast evaluation, separately from the journal citation. Difficulty predicting a historical sample does not prove that every market and period is unpredictable."}};export{e as default};
